# 07-LPG / landing pages

**Goes here.** What a page does and in what order. Page types, section order, above
the fold, image sequence and the job of each slot, copy principles on the page, proof
placement, objection handling, mobile specifics, friction removal.

## Page types, all of which live here

Standard product page, advertorial, listicle, quiz funnel, comparison page, long form
sales page, VSL page.

**Advertorials and quiz funnels are page types.** They were being filed in 11-ADC,
10-MCR and 06-MEA because the titles mention ads, copy or conversion. They belong
here. The question is always: is this about the page the visitor lands on? If yes,
it is LPG.

## Not here

- Whether a page change actually worked -> 09-CRO
- How fast the page loads -> 08-SPD
- Brand voice rules -> 04-BRD
- Discovering which objections exist -> 02-AVT
- Ad copy and general copywriting craft -> 11-ADC
- An Amazon listing -> 22-AMZ

**The LPG and CRO line.** LPG is what a good page does. CRO is whether a change to it
was real. "Put the sizing comparison above the fold" is LPG. "You need 400 conversions
a month to A/B test that, here is the stopping rule" is CRO.

A source titled "CRO" that is really a list of page changes belongs HERE. Most
YouTube CRO content is page tactics with no statistics in it. The test is simple: does
it mention sample size, significance or a stopping rule? If not, it is LPG.

