## Topics

page types and section order, above the fold, image sequence and slot jobs, copy
principles, proof placement, objection handling, mobile specifics, friction removal,
advertorial structure, quiz funnel structure, comparison and listicle structures.

## Look for

Section order and what each section does. What must be above the fold. The exact
image sequence and the job of each slot. Where proof goes and why. Mobile differences.
For advertorials: the section order and the transition into the product. For quiz
funnels: question count, result logic, and the drop-off per step.

## Skip

Design trend content. Aesthetics with no conversion argument. Dropshipping funnels,
which are an explicit skip in any folder.

## Twyman's law applies hard in this folder

This folder attracts revenue-claim titles: "$535k a month", "$1.3m a month using AI",
"20% conversions, 10x the average". A number in a title is marketing for the video.
Extract the structure and the method. Never card the headline number. A 20% site
conversion claim should be treated as an instrumentation error until shown otherwise.

## AI tooling demos

Several sources here are "write advertorials with Claude in 6 minutes". Keep the page
structure they use, drop the tool workflow. Tool steps decay in months.

## Scope mix

Large baseline component: page structure, image set, trust elements, friction
removal.

## Done when

You can describe 6 page types, their section orders, and which avatar and offer each
